<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Personal Combined Feed</title><link>https://example.invalid</link><description>Personal aggregate feed</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:24:25 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Show HN: Zero Shot – Energy Drink for You and Your AI Agents</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49522983</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hey HN! I built &lt;a href="https://zeroshothq.dev/" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://zeroshothq.dev/&lt;/a&gt;, an energy drink for AI engineers, ordered through an API.&lt;p&gt;Zero Shot is designed only for tech people who needs caffeine but in a healthy way. Every flavour is named after a paper: the label prints the title, year and arXiv number.&lt;p&gt;Does Claude tells you to go to sleep too? The first batch gives you a SKILL.md to wake up your AI agents.&lt;p&gt;The API is live if you want to poke at it:
curl "&lt;a href="https://api.zeroshothq.dev/12?email=you@company.com" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://api.zeroshothq.dev/12?email=you@company.com&lt;/a&gt;"&lt;p&gt;Happy to chat about product. Let me know if you have questions/comments/feature requests!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comments URL: &lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49522983"&gt;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49522983&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Points: 1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49522983</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:06:11 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Selfship.ai – Surface and fix isues with your agentic applications 24x7</title><link>https://selfship.ai/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;We've been building an AI chat based trading system for last 3 years. The biggest issue was that when our Agent would mess up, we wouldn't know until a user reported. Agent traces helped us uncover what's wrong. But surfacing issues was almost always a manual trigger. So from those learnings, we built Selfship.ai. It's an autonomous system that observes every trace/turn/multi turn convo to find out issues. If a user got what they wanted, if a tool call is failing repeatedly, if users have to always reframe their questions, if the agent is taking optimal paths and many more. It's a loop - group failures by user intent, evaluate them, and ship fixes as PRs. After a fix is deployed, it evaluates if it worked or not. We recently opened it up as a SaaS. 
If you have an agentic product in production, we would love for you to try it out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
